GAL22V10
UA6RACP

AB1 AB2 AB3 AB4 AB5 AB6 GALSTB RCFG8 RCFG4 RCFG2 BASEA GND
RW CFGIN NC15 ACPHASE RST DB15 DB14 DB13 DB12 NC22 DRVEN VCC

; =====================================================================
; UA6 - RocHard RH800C  -  b001d base latch + DRIVE /_AC_PHASE LOW
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; IDENTICAL to ua6_hd_b001d.pld (stable: base latch (0,0,1), HD boots,
; RAM window at $200000) EXCEPT /_AC_PHASE (pin 16) is now DRIVEN LOW
; instead of Hi-Z.
;
; WHY (LA-proven 2026-08-05, rcotec_ram_latchclk.csv):
;   The RAM SELECT chain is dead: /BASE_A, /BASE_B and /_UA3SEL NEVER
;   assert (0 low samples in 12M) while /_LATCH_CLK toggles fine. Both
;   U11 and U12 are ORIGINAL working chips, so the logic exists - an
;   INPUT is blocking the state machine.
;   Netlist: /_AC_PHASE is driven by EXACTLY ONE source = UA6 pin 16.
;   Every ua6_hd clone left p16 Hi-Z -> U11 pin 5 (/_AC_PHASE) FLOATS
;   HIGH (confirmed on LA: AC_PHASE high whole trace, /_LATCH_EN never
;   asserts). U11's readable (HD-path) outputs don't use AC_PHASE -> HD
;   works floating; but its two UNREADABLE outputs /_UA3SEL (o17) and
;   /_LATCH_EN (o19) = exactly the two dead RAM-path signals. If o17/o19
;   need /_AC_PHASE, floating it kills ONLY the RAM select. Matches all
;   symptoms.
;   Original UA6 black-box crack showed it drives p16 LOW -> low is at
;   least the resting level U11's RAM path expects, and it is HD-safe
;   (the original board runs HD with AC_PHASE low). Earlier "AC_PHASE
;   low red-screened" was a PRE-base-latch build; retry now.
;
; DISCRIMINATOR:
;   - RAM select starts working (/_UA3SEL asserts + DTACK) => U11 needed
;     a LEVEL (low). Possible full fix.
;   - Still hangs, /_UA3SEL still high => U11 needs a PHASE (pulse/edge);
;     AC_PHASE must be DYNAMIC. Derive its timing (vs _AS/_GALSTROBE/
;     _CDAC) from the capture and build the dynamic variant next.
;
; BOARD: game II - DIP-1 ON - DIP-2 ON - JPA1 2M.
;   Test 1 (RAM off): HD must still boot (AC_PHASE low is HD-safe).
;   Test 2 (RAM on, SIMMs in bank0): does /_UA3SEL assert at $200000?
; =====================================================================


; ---- /_DRVEN (pin 23) : UNCHANGED working latched version -----------
/DRVEN = /CFGIN & /BASEA & RST
       + /CFGIN & /DRVEN & RST


; ---- /_AC_PHASE (pin 16) : DRIVE LOW (was Hi-Z) ---------------------
; ACPHASE declared active-high (no slash). .T = tautological-false ->
; output data = 0 -> pin LOW. .E = VCC -> always enabled (always driven).
ACPHASE.T = AB1 & /AB1
ACPHASE.E = VCC


; ---- DB13 (pin 20) + DB12 (pin 21) : Hi-Z ---------------------------
DB13.T = VCC
DB13.E = AB1 & /AB1
DB12.T = VCC
DB12.E = AB1 & /AB1

; ---- DB15 (pin 18) + DB14 (pin 19) : drive LOW while /_DRVEN off -----
; DB15 -> o16 (UA4.16), DB14 -> o17 (UA4.17). .E = DRVEN (whole oe-off
; window) so UA4 captures/holds o16=0, o17=0 -> base latch (0,0,1).
DB15.T = AB1 & /AB1
DB15.E = DRVEN
DB14.T = AB1 & /AB1
DB14.E = DRVEN


; ---- NC15 (pin 15), NC22 (pin 22) : Hi-Z (unchanged) ----------------
NC15.T = VCC
NC15.E = AB1 & /AB1
NC22.T = VCC
NC22.E = AB1 & /AB1


DESCRIPTION

UA6 HD build + base-latch->(0,0,1) + /_AC_PHASE (pin16) DRIVEN LOW.

Same as ua6_hd_b001d except pin 16 (/_AC_PHASE) is actively driven LOW
instead of left Hi-Z. LA proved the RAM-select chain (/BASE_A, /BASE_B,
/_UA3SEL) never asserts because /_AC_PHASE - the only qualifier U11's
RAM-path outputs (o17/o19) get from UA6 - was floating high (UA6 clone
never drove p16). Original UA6 drives p16 low (black-box crack) and it
is HD-safe. This restores that level to test whether U11's RAM select
needs a LEVEL (low) or a dynamic PHASE.

TEST:
  1. RAM off: HD still boots (must - AC_PHASE low matches original).
  2. RAM on, SIMMs bank0: /_UA3SEL assert at $200000 write? DTACK back?
     ATK memory test pass (or at least not instant-hang)?
